#!/bin/sh
# PX4 parameters for every swarm member. PX4's own init script applies them: after the
# airframe, init.d-posix/rcS sources the first `px4-rc.params` on PATH ("user defined
# params for instances can be in PATH"), and docker/entrypoint.sh puts this directory at
# the front of every instance's PATH. `param set-default` is how PX4's airframes set
# theirs, so a value someone sets by hand (QGroundControl, `param set`) still wins.
# shellcheck disable=SC2154

# Height reference: the barometer (0), not GNSS (1, PX4 v1.15's default). In simulation
# the barometer is the steadier of the two: the x500 model's pressure sensor carries
# 0.01 Pa of noise, while sensor_gps_sim adds 0.5 m of white noise to every GNSS altitude
# sample. GNSS height is still fused; the EKF estimates its offset as a bias.
#
# What this does NOT do is put a drone's local zero on its pad — with either reference,
# PX4 fixes the local origin's altitude from whatever height its estimator had reached
# when the first GNSS fix passed its checks, and the SITL smoke saw pads read up to 2.6 m
# off. Heights are measured from PX4's home instead (swarm_coordination/frames.py).
param set-default EKF2_HGT_REF 0
